## Re-login checklist

Complete after Linux apps are installed and network access is ready.

- [ ] Browser sync/account sign-in (Brave/Edge/Chrome/Firefox as applicable)
- [ ] Password manager / Google Password Manager / vault unlock
- [ ] Email/calendar accounts
- [ ] Messaging/collaboration apps (Slack/Discord/Teams/etc.)
- [ ] Developer services (GitHub/GitLab, package registries, cloud CLIs) — **new
      sign-ins/tokens only; do not reuse copied secrets**
- [ ] IDE/editor sync or settings import (VS Code/etc.)
- [ ] MFA devices/authenticator access verified (have recovery path ready)
- [ ] Backup/sync clients (Nextcloud/Drive/rclone/etc.) reviewed and reconnected
- [ ] License/entitlement sign-ins (if applicable)

## Dev environment setup

- [ ] Git installed; `user.name`/`user.email` verified
- [ ] `.gitconfig` reviewed and restored safely (no credential helper secrets)
- [ ] SSH: generate new keys or manually install approved keys; test remotes
- [ ] Node.js: install required version (distro/nvm/fnm/volta/Nix as appropriate)
- [ ] Node projects: run dependency install from lockfiles (no `node_modules` copy)
- [ ] Python: install required version; recreate venvs from manifests/lockfiles
- [ ] Go: install required version; verify `go env`, PATH, and module access
- [ ] Docker/Podman: install using distro-supported method; recreate compose/env
      files **after reviewing secrets**
- [ ] Editors/IDEs: reinstall extensions; fix paths, shells, SDKs, linters
- [ ] Project-specific build tools, databases, and local services reinstalled

## Manual actions

